---
title: Registration & Email Verification
---
%% Sign-up creates a DISABLED account. Only the emailed link enables it, which is what stops
%% one person registering an address they don't control.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>RegisterComponent
    participant API as UserController<br/>/user/register
    participant SVC as UserService
    participant DB as MySQL
    participant MAIL as EmailService
    participant EV as NewUserEventListener

    U->>SPA: First name, last name, email, password
    SPA->>SPA: Client-side PasswordPolicy check
    note left of SPA: UX only — the backend re-validates<br/>with the identical pattern regardless<br/>of what the client sends.

    SPA->>API: POST /user/register
    API->>SVC: createUser(form)
    SVC->>SVC: Re-validate password server-side

    alt email already registered
        SVC-->>API: conflict
        API-->>SPA: Generic failure — same shape as any other
        note right of API: Must not confirm the address is taken.
    else new address
        SVC->>DB: INSERT users (enabled = FALSE, non_locked = TRUE)<br/>password BCrypt strength 12
        SVC->>DB: Assign the default role
        SVC->>DB: INSERT accountverifications (url key)
        SVC->>MAIL: Send verification link<br/>{UI_APP_URL}/verify/account/{key}
        SVC->>EV: Publish registration event
        EV->>DB: Write the audit row
        note right of EV: Audit failures are swallowed and logged,<br/>never rethrown — Spring's synchronous<br/>multicaster would otherwise turn a failed<br/>audit write into a failed registration.
        API-->>SPA: 201 — "check your email"
    end

    U->>U: Open email, click the link
    U->>SPA: Navigate /verify/account/{key}
    SPA->>API: GET /user/verify/account/{key}
    API->>DB: Look up the key

    alt key valid
        API->>DB: UPDATE users SET enabled = TRUE
        API->>DB: Delete the verification row — single use
        API-->>SPA: 200 — account active
        SPA->>U: Redirect to /login
    else expired or unknown
        API-->>SPA: 400 — link no longer valid
    end

    note over U, EV: Seeded demo accounts skip all of this: DemoDataSeeder inserts them<br/>already enabled, which is why they exist only on the dev profile.
